      "lineNbr": 57,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-01-20T11:30:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It definitely look easier to use, although I can live with this.\n\nrand::random is reseeded from the OS every 64k (https://docs.rs/rand/latest/rand/rngs/struct.ThreadRng.html), whereas the Ring SystemRandom calls the OS for every byte (https://briansmith.org/rustdoc/ring/rand/struct.SystemRandom.html).\n\nThe latter seems marginally preferable?",
      "parentUuid": "bd3f0411_e93084f1",
      "revId": "80c4d9a1485bc878915820aae631ad3821639f66",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
