    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0427308c_79cc2338",
        "filename": "compos/src/blob_encryptor.rs",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 66,
      "author": {
        "id": 1139038
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-01-19T19:36:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Example serialized format from KM [1]: \u003cversion byte\u003e \u003cnonce\u003e \u003cciphertext + tag\u003e \u003cKM things\u003e\n\nso basically just reordered with a version number\n\n[1] -- http://cs/android/system/keymaster/key_blob_utils/auth_encrypted_key_blob.cpp;l\u003d209;rcl\u003d0c007cd31d6f8a2258ca797732648734a4884a09",
      "parentUuid": "49a8f154_ce55b464",
      "revId": "80c4d9a1485bc878915820aae631ad3821639f66",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f0f45301_ce1c3bf3",
        "filename": "compos/src/blob_encryptor.rs",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 66,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-01-20T11:30:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I put the nonce at the end purely because it made it slightly easier to write the code. But I figured out how to fix that.\n\nI don\u0027t think we need versioning - the key should always be consumed by exactly the same version of CompOS that wrote it; if there\u0027s a version mismatch then the compilation didn\u0027t do the right thing anyway so failure is fine.",
      "parentUuid": "0427308c_79cc2338",
      "revId": "80c4d9a1485bc878915820aae631ad3821639f66",
